## 1. Core Identity & Authorization Distinction

To avoid architectural dead-ends and rigid code branches (`if (user.role === 'HR')`), we separate five fundamental concepts across the entire system:

| Dimension | Concept | Purpose | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Job Title** | Designation | What the person does in the company organizational chart | *Senior Software Engineer, VP Operations, HR Executive* |
| **2. System Role** | Named Role | A bundle of permissions assigned to a user within their tenant | *Company Admin, HR Manager, Team Lead, Attendance Officer* |
| **3. Permissions** | Atomic Capabilities | Granular action privileges granted by assigned roles | `employee.create`, `leave.approve`, `payroll.process` |
| **4. Operational Manager** | Team Lead (TL) | Day-to-day work supervisor for rosters, shift attendance, and L1 approvals | *Team Lead - Mobile Eng* |
| **5. Administrative Manager** | Reporting Manager | Line manager responsible for appraisals, L2 approvals, and team escalations | *Engineering Manager / Director* |

