### Table Definitions & Foreign Key Isolation

1. **`organizations`** (`tenant_id` PK): Legal entity, domain, plan tier, status, RLS tenant isolation root.
2. **`users`** (`id`, `tenant_id`, `email`, `password_hash`, `status`, `employee_id`): Authentication identity (shared across Web & Mobile).
3. **`roles`** (`id`, `tenant_id`, `name`, `description`, `is_system`, `created_at`): System and custom roles defined per tenant.
4. **`permissions`** (`code`, `module`, `action`, `description`): Global permission catalog (e.g. `attendance.approve`, `payroll.process`).
5. **`role_permissions`** (`id`, `role_id`, `permission_code`, `scope_level`): Mapping of roles to granular capabilities and data scopes.
6. **`user_roles`** (`id`, `user_id`, `role_id`, `tenant_id`): Multi-role assignment per user.
7. **`employees`** (`id`, `tenant_id`, `employee_code`, `department_id`, `designation_id`, `reporting_manager_id`, `team_lead_id`, `shift_id`, `status`): Physical workforce profile.
8. **`approval_workflows`** (`id`, `tenant_id`, `module`, `levels_json`): Dynamic multi-tier approval paths (TL -> Manager -> HR).

